WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:15.274
Edmund and Goneril rode up to her castle and were met by Oswald.

2
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:22.453
"Madam, I must warn you," he said. "Your husband takes the king's side. He does not want to fight the French."

3
00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:28.191
"He is a weakling," Goneril fumed. She smiled invitingly at Edmund.

4
00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:33.024
"Not like you, fair Edmund." She kissed him on the forehead.

5
00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:38.888
"Now, return to my sister and Cornwall. I will soon send word to you."

6
00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:44.158
After Edmund rode away, the gates opened and the Duke of Albany strode out.

7
00:00:44.159 --> 00:00:51.483
"Goneril," he cried, "what have you and your sister done to your father? You are tigers, not daughters!"

8
00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:59.261
"Silence, you coward!" Goneril retorted. "Cordelia and the French army are at Dover—we are at war!"

9
00:00:59.262 --> 00:01:05.791
"If the French have invaded British soil, then I must fight," said Albany unhappily.

10
00:01:05.792 --> 00:01:11.601
They were interrupted by a messenger on horseback. "The Duke of Cornwall is dead!" he shouted.

11
00:01:11.602 --> 00:01:16.434
"Slain by a servant who tried to stop him from putting out Gloucester's eyes!"

12
00:01:16.435 --> 00:01:20.338
"Where was Edmund when this was happening?" asked Albany.

13
00:01:20.339 --> 00:01:24.881
"Gone, sir. It was he who informed against his father."

14
00:01:24.882 --> 00:01:33.754
"Cornwall is dead?" thought Goneril. "Then my sister is free to remarry. And she will soon see my Edmund. I don't like this."

15
00:01:33.755 --> 00:01:38.416
Goneril quickly formed a plan. She went inside and wrote a letter.

16
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:44.448
"Take this to Edmund," she commanded Oswald. "And if you see Gloucester, kill him.

17
00:01:44.449 --> 00:01:50.202
He stirs up too much sympathy and makes us look bad. We will meet you in Dover."

18
00:01:50.203 --> 00:01:59.804
Edgar and Gloucester were nearing Dover when they encountered Lear, dressed in strange clothing, with wildflowers in his hair and around his neck.

19
00:01:59.805 --> 00:02:06.761
"I am the king himself!" Lear babbled. "Look, a mouse! They flattered me like a dog . . ."

20
00:02:06.762 --> 00:02:12.434
"I know that voice!" exclaimed Gloucester. "My lord, do you know who I am?"

21
00:02:12.435 --> 00:02:18.436
Lear stared at Gloucester's empty eye sockets. At last, he said, "You are Gloucester."

22
00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:27.579
At that moment, Cordelia's servants arrived. "The queen of France wants us to bring her father to her," one said, and they led the king away.

23
00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.196
Then Edgar saw Oswald approaching.

24
00:02:31.197 --> 00:02:37.617
"Traitor, you must die!" Oswald shouted at Gloucester, his hand on his sword.

25
00:02:37.618 --> 00:02:42.554
Moving quickly, Edgar drew his knife and stabbed Oswald in the chest.

26
00:02:42.555 --> 00:02:52.039
Oswald fell and whispered, "Take my purse and deliver the letter inside to Edmund, Earl of Gloucester. I am dying . . ."

27
00:02:52.040 --> 00:03:01.903
Edgar's eyes widened as he read the letter. "I must warn Albany! Goneril wants Edmund to kill her husband. Then she will marry Edmund."

28
00:03:01.904 --> 00:03:10.072
At the French camp, Cordelia's doctors had given Lear a potion to calm him. He lay sleeping as Cordelia watched over him.

29
00:03:10.073 --> 00:03:18.485
At last, Lear opened his eyes. "Am I in my right mind?" he murmured. "Are you my child Cordelia?"

30
00:03:18.486 --> 00:03:23.342
"I am," she said, weeping and tenderly taking his hand.

31
00:03:23.343 --> 00:03:28.790
"I am very foolish," said Lear. "I must ask your forgiveness."

32
00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:36.187
Meanwhile, at the British camp in Dover, Regan had asked Edmund to lead her army, since Cornwall was dead.

33
00:03:36.188 --> 00:03:41.179
"I wish to marry you," Regan said, "but are you in love with Goneril?"

34
00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:49.655
"By my honor, no," answered Edmund. To himself, he said, "Both sisters want me. I'll turn this to my advantage!"

35
00:03:49.656 --> 00:03:59.313
In another part of the camp, Edgar, now disguised as a peasant, approached Albany and handed him the letter he'd taken from Oswald.

36
00:03:59.314 --> 00:04:08.369
"Your life is in danger," Edgar said. "If you win the battle, sound your trumpets and a knight will come to prove what this letter contains."

37
00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:15.290
The battle began early the next morning. It was short and bloody, and the French forces were defeated.

38
00:04:15.291 --> 00:04:19.626
Lear and Cordelia were captured and brought to the British camp.

39
00:04:19.627 --> 00:04:27.586
"Take them to the prison," Edmund ordered an army captain and handed him a note. "Follow these instructions, and you will be rewarded."

40
00:04:27.587 --> 00:04:32.674
As the captain led Cordelia and the king away, Cordelia was heartbroken.

41
00:04:32.675 --> 00:04:43.228
But her father tried to comfort her, saying, "In prison, we'll be like two birds in a cage. We'll sing and pray and laugh and tell old tales."

42
00:04:43.229 --> 00:04:48.165
When Albany heard Lear and Cordelia were in prison, he was furious.

43
00:04:48.172 --> 00:04:54.704
"Edmund," he said, "that decision was not yours to make. You are not my equal in rank."

44
00:04:54.706 --> 00:05:00.602
"He led my army," Regan interrupted. "I declare him my lord and master."

45
00:05:00.603 --> 00:05:05.150
Jealous, Goneril jumped in. "Will you marry him?"

46
00:05:05.151 --> 00:05:14.380
"Not so fast," said Albany. "I arrest you for treason, Edmund, and Goneril too. You planned to kill me and get married!"

47
00:05:14.381 --> 00:05:17.602
"You have no proof," Goneril shot back.

48
00:05:17.603 --> 00:05:24.307
Regan looked pale and weak. "I am not well," she whispered. Two servants led her away.

49
00:05:24.308 --> 00:05:29.522
"I will defend my honor," Edmund declared. "Who challenges me?"

50
00:05:29.523 --> 00:05:35.252
Suddenly, Edgar appeared in the armor of a knight, his face hidden by his helmet.

51
00:05:35.253 --> 00:05:43.054
"Edmund," he cried, "you are a traitor against your father, your brother, and the Duke of Albany!"

52
00:05:43.055 --> 00:05:48.919
The two men drew their swords and fought. Edgar finally struck Edmund down.

53
00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:54.891
Goneril ran to him. "Edmund," she shrieked, "are you badly hurt?"

54
00:05:54.892 --> 00:06:03.042
"Enough, Goneril," said Albany sternly and held out the letter she'd written to Edmund. "Here is proof of your wickedness!"

55
00:06:03.043 --> 00:06:11.502
"What do I care?" Goneril said haughtily, but there was a desperate look in her eyes. She rushed away to the tent she shared with her sister.

56
00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:18.661
Edgar removed his helmet and knelt beside Edmund, who struggled to breathe. Remorse washed over the dying man.

57
00:06:18.662 --> 00:06:27.145
"Brother," Edmund said, "I have done all you accuse me of, and more. May you and our father forgive me . . ."

58
00:06:27.146 --> 00:06:36.060
"Alas," Edgar said, "our father has died." Edgar related how he had disguised himself and then met up with Gloucester.

59
00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:43.232
"When I finally revealed myself to him this morning, he was overjoyed. But the shock stopped his poor heart."

60
00:06:43.233 --> 00:06:47.580
Just then a messenger ran toward them, carrying a bloody knife.

61
00:06:47.581 --> 00:06:55.963
"My lady Goneril is dead, by her own hand," he cried. "And she confessed to poisoning her sister, who is dead too!"

62
00:06:55.964 --> 00:07:03.687
"This is also my fault." gasped Edmund. "They both wanted to marry me. But maybe I can finally do some good.

63
00:07:03.694 --> 00:07:14.041
I secretly ordered Lear and Cordelia to be killed. Send someone to the prison to stop the executions!" Edmund said, right before he died.

64
00:07:14.042 --> 00:07:22.247
But it was too late. Within moments, Lear appeared, carrying Cordelia's body. The faithful Kent followed behind him.

65
00:07:22.248 --> 00:07:28.424
"She's gone forever!" wailed the king. "Curses on you murderers!"

66
00:07:28.425 --> 00:07:33.815
He looked up and saw Kent. "Are you not Kent?" he asked, confused.

67
00:07:33.816 --> 00:07:42.442
"Sir, I am," Kent replied. "I am also Caius. I chose to stay with you through all your trials."

68
00:07:42.443 --> 00:07:48.760
"Good Kent, you are welcome here," said Lear. He looked at his daughter's face again.

69
00:07:48.761 --> 00:07:57.309
"Oh, Cordelia, why should a dog, a horse, a rat have life, and you no breath at all?"

70
00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:03.524
The death of his innocent child was too much to bear. Lear plunged into madness again.

71
00:08:03.525 --> 00:08:09.787
"Look," he whispered, imagining she was still alive. "Her lips, they move . . . !"

72
00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:15.872
Then Lear, his heart broken, took one final breath and fell to the ground.

73
00:08:15.873 --> 00:08:24.221
"He is gone," said Kent, gazing down at the master he had served so loyally. "It is a wonder he endured so long."

74
00:08:24.222 --> 00:08:28.856
"All is woe in the kingdom now," murmured Albany.

75
00:08:28.857 --> 00:08:37.207
"The oldest have suffered most," said Edgar. "Surely, we who are young will never see such misery again."
